Build a numerical validation argument across several kinds of evidence (@rc-numericaltests: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @reproducible-computation, #source "../sources/Good-Research-Code.lingua#r_771ZMSHAY1TCSTFCHPT9KZRA66", #source "../sources/Numerical-and-Random-Contracts.lingua#r_22SKS09JTH3YF4244RX2FYWHNY", #source "../sources/Floating-Point-Goldberg.lingua#r_4FHXH9WWX5Q535CD32ESSVSEHH", #reproducible-computation "../performance/Measure-before-optimizing.lingua#r_4YB1P59S34RAHN5YHNDTSDZH8Q", #general-chemistry "../../../stem/chemistry/general-chemistry/equilibrium/An-inspectable-equilibrium-solver.lingua#r_0228516WK8JJ014E9XC51TNZZY", #geology "../../../nature/earth/geology/structures/An-inspectable-three-point-plane.lingua#r_1X60JZT3S9BPQQ5B2J4BFDRCW9", #mineralogy-and-petrology "../../../nature/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/equilibrium/An-inspectable-two-phase-equilibrium.lingua#r_0N9KF8HD8HGNAZ114DPF9ZP2JW", #mining-and-mineral-engineering "../../../stem/engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/planning/An-exhaustively-checkable-small-mine-schedule.lingua#r_53F79J4H9V3K4WT935QA0KHDD7", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "../../../ergon/materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/kinetics/An-inspectable-conservative-diffusion-calculation.lingua#r_2SMK31412VCY92Z6GTYZGYG9YM", #industrial-chemistry "../../../stem/chemistry/industrial-chemistry/balances/An-inspectable-recycle-and-purge-account.lingua#r_7DBH60P2MM84PVRAC802SEW9KZ", #chemical-supply-systems "../../../ergon/materials/chemical-feedstocks-and-supply-systems/inventory/An-inspectable-lot-release-and-expiry-account.lingua#r_684PQX9EQBD1WDF7XP6FMWJCD6", #electromagnetism "../../../stem/physics/electromagnetism/computation/An-inspectable-conservative-electrostatic-solver.lingua#r_5M84JGBFDFE7QQVSBX3S0TMASK", #electrical-power-engineering "../../../stem/engineering/electrical-power-engineering/computation/An-inspectable-two-bus-AC-power-flow.lingua#r_4NH5W4H1B5YARD5V8V1J3MX7G9", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../../../stem/physics/thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer/computation/An-inspectable-conservative-transient-layered-slab.lingua#r_6B5B7E7C3Z1APY0RYAC09P12ET", #fluid-dynamics "../../../stem/physics/fluid-dynamics/computation/Verify-fluid-code-before-comparing-it-with-an-experiment.lingua#r_56BN593RTAZZVHY7S5VT2EJRKK") { r_7EY9S6DXHFHSJAGA30W35A4ZD8
**Read:** [The Good Research Code Handbook — Mineault and community](../sources/Good-Research-Code.lingua#r_771ZMSHAY1TCSTFCHPT9KZRA66), the complete numerical-testing extension and its project; [Numerical arrays and reproducible random streams — NumPy documentation](../sources/Numerical-and-Random-Contracts.lingua#r_22SKS09JTH3YF4244RX2FYWHNY), array, dtype, broadcasting, testing, and reduction contracts actually used; [What Every Computer Scientist Should Know About Floating-Point Arithmetic — Goldberg](../sources/Floating-Point-Goldberg.lingua#r_4FHXH9WWX5Q535CD32ESSVSEHH), the complete paper reviewed against the study.

Combine independent evidence rather than making every check a comparison with one trusted program. An analytic case, exact arithmetic on a small input, dimensional analysis, limiting behavior, conservation, convergence, alternative algorithms, and carefully chosen adversarial examples answer different questions. Record what each test can and cannot establish.

Build a table for the two-lot balance, the decay approximation, the cancellation example, and the squared-uniform simulation. For each state the mathematical specification, expected value or relation, implementation boundary, comparison rule, and observed result. A tolerance justified for an exponential approximation should not be copied into a mass-conservation check that is exact in rational arithmetic.

Inspect array shapes, broadcasting, units, dtype promotion, reduction order, missing-value handling, and nonfinite values in a NumPy extension. An incorrect shape can yield a plausible matrix of answers instead of the intended vector. Check the smallest hand-calculable cases before optimizing or running a large study. A package's test suite does not test your interpretation of its API.

**Work:** independently implement one benchmark without calling the original calculation helper. Deliberately introduce a unit/basis error, an unstable expression, an excessive step, and a repeated-stream defect. Explain which checks detect each and which remain blind. Repair the implementation and preserve the independently justified regression cases.

Then extend one numerical problem until no exact full answer is available. Use a hierarchy of simpler known cases, convergence evidence, parameter sensitivity, and independent comparison to defend a bounded accuracy claim. Relate the numerical error budget to [Model discrepancy, double counting, and sensitivity to assumptions](../../metrology/uncertainty/Model-discrepancy-and-robustness.lingua#r_13PJ61YH29120EKV42ZT1SQTG3) and the uncertainties of the intended use. Numerical validation is part of the research argument; it is not a certificate that every downstream scientific conclusion follows.

